  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></math>,&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is continuous&nbsp;function in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>]</mo></math> such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;for all&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8804;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> for all&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>]</mo></math>.</p><p>The largest possible interval in which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math> lies&nbsp;is :</p>",
